course: dictionary
lesson: 9369
title: Spooky: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Spooky has more than one meaning, so the words around it show you which one to use. «Spooky stories are fun because your brain is a brilliant pattern-finder: in the dark it turns a coat into a figure.» Here spooky means strange and a bit frightening, the feeling you get in the dark.
explain: Clues also show when spooky is not about ghosts. She puts the radio on «so it's not spooky». The radio is on to stop a strange, scary feeling. In everyday talk, «that's spooky» can be said about a coincidence, like two friends wearing the same shirt: it is odd and surprising, not frightening.
explain: Animals can be spooky too. A spooky horse is easily frightened or nervous, so it jumps at a plastic bag. When you meet spooky, swap in another word, such as frightening or surprising, and see which one still makes sense.
fact: Spooky means strange and a bit frightening, as if there might be ghosts.
fact: Informally, spooky can mean strangely surprising, like an odd coincidence: «that's spooky».
fact: Informally, an animal that is spooky is easily frightened or nervous.
fact: Spookier and spookiest are the comparison forms: a spookier story, the spookiest house on the street.
fact: Snakes have no outer ears and no eyelids, so the snake charmer's cobra only looks spooky; it hears little of the flute.
exercise: «Spooky stories are fun because your brain is a brilliant pattern-finder.» What does spooky mean here? | Bright and sunny | Very tidy and clean | Tired and hungry | *Strange and a bit frightening, as if there might be ghosts
exercise: Ella says, «That's spooky, we both got the same birthday present!» What does spooky mean here? | *Strangely surprising, like an odd coincidence | Very loud | Full of ghosts | Frightened of the dark
exercise: A spooky horse is one that is what? | Painted with spots | Very fast and strong | Asleep all day | *Easily frightened or nervous
test: The radio was on «so it's not spooky». What was the writer trying to stop? | *A strange, scary feeling | Loud music | Hunger | Rain on the window
test: Which word is the comparison form of spooky, used to compare two things? | Spooky | *Spookier | Spook | Spookily
exam: Jayden reads «a spooky coincidence» and asks what it means. Which meaning fits best? | *Strangely surprising, like an odd coincidence | Very frightening, like a ghost film | Easily frightened | Very bright
